      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is reported as open today, with superb snow conditions and coverage following recent fresh snow and a cold, calm, clear night. The mountain is offering exceptional cord, while off-piste skiing is also in good shape after recent top operations. Current conditions are 1°C with 5 km/h winds and 8 km/h gusts, with much colder temperatures arriving Thursday and stronger winds developing toward the weekend. Main Basin and Valley View are scheduled to open at 8:30 am, followed by Captains, Willows, Soho and T-Bar at 9:00 am. The mountain's live status panel is currently showing the lifts and terrain as closed, conflicting with the more recent Mountain Manager update stating that the resort is open and identifying today's scheduled openings. (Issued: 12:30 pm, 8 Sep) The JWI Big Air event is scheduled for 10:00 am, with viewing and access from Skyline. The Olympic Pipe is scheduled to close at 1:30 pm, while the Platter will continue operating for the JWI Big Air event. Access roads are chain free, although chains must always be carried, and an active road-hazard advisory remains in place. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 10 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
